"""Function Keys - Linux port of 3Dconnexion's "Function Keys" LCD applet
(3DxLCD10SPPRO.exe) for the SpacePilot PRO.

Like the original it reads LCDCfg.xml - the file the driver writes with the
focused application, the motion filters, an info line (button just pressed,
speed) and the text of every button - and draws it on three pages:

  1. keys 1-5, with the long-press keys 6-10 in blue
  2. the view keys (T/B, F/BK, R/L, ISO1/ISO2, Roll +/-)
  3. SHIFT ESC CTRL ALT MENU, speed -/+, Pan/Zoom, Dominant, Rotation, FIT

LEFT / RIGHT switch pages. 3dxlinuxd writes the file to /run/3dxlinux/LCDCfg.xml
(lcd_cfg in 3dxlinux.conf). The artwork comes from the original applet when it has
been extracted from the 3DxWare installer (3dxlinux-extract-3dxware-ui).
"""

